## Quickstart
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

### Basic Installation
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

Install directly from the repository:

{% set pip_uri="git+" + mkdocs.config.site_source_url + "@" + mkdocs.config.pip_default_version %}

```bash {.cli_example}

# Typical install
$ pip install \
  "mcmas @ {{pip_uri}}"

# Optional AI Stuff: camel, openai
$ pip install \
  "mcmas[ai] @ {{pip_uri}}"

# Other Experimental Stuff: pymodelchecking
$ pip install \
  "mcmas[ai] @ {{pip_uri}}"
```

### Running with Docker
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

See [this section](#for-developers) for details about building/testing the container.

```bash {.cli_example}
# Pull the container
$ docker pull ghcr.io/mattvonrocketstein/py-mcmas:main
```

Note that the docker container for pymcmas still uses docker to interact with the `mcmas` engine!  So you'll want to share the socket.  Usually you'll also want a volume for the working directory to share files.

```bash {.cli_example}
# Run spec from file
$ docker run -it \
	-v `pwd`:/tests -w /tests \
	-v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
	ghcr.io/mattvonrocketstein/py-mcmas:main \
		./tests/data/minimal.ispl
```

Note that the default entrypoint for the container is the [`ispl`]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/cli#ispl) command, but the [`mcmas` command]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/cli#mcmas) is also available.
{#
### Requirements
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

Platforms used in development include recentish docker, recentish make (*3.8+*) and bash (*5+*) on both Linux and MacOS.  Testing done in CI only uses Linux and won't try every possible combination of versions, but the goal is to support most things you'll encounter in the wild.
#}

### For Developers
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

For development on `compose.mk` itself, here's how you can clone the project, build related containers, and run the test suites.

```bash {.cli_example}
# Clone
$ git clone {{mkdocs.config.site_source_url}}

# Build docs
$ make docs

# Do everything else
$ make clean init normalize validate test

# Build pymcmas container
$ make docker.pymcmas.build

# Run main test-suite, inside the container
$ make docker.pymcmas.test
```

